<title>UK: Barclays active, talk of share buy back.</title>
<headline>Barclays active, talk of share buy back.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Barclays Plc rose on Tuesday in active trade amid talk that the company had been buying back more shares.</p>
<p>Volume in the the shares jumped to 26 million compared with around two million shares traded on Monday.  </p>
<p>The shares were 12-1/2p higher at 11.06-1/2 stg by 1431 GMT.</p>
<p>Traders noted that large chunks of stock had changed hands at a price of 10.96-1/2 stg earlier on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;Clearly, something special has taken place,&quot; one dealer said.&quot;This activity does seem to suggest there has been a buy back exercise.&quot;</p>
</text>
